  "wikitext": "{{PageDisplay}}\n[[File:Goat.png|200px|left|Goat]]\n\n{{Infobox\n |title = [[Animals|Animal]]\n |level = 32 • 37 • 50\n |price = 2,150 • 5,400 • 8,650\n |gives = {{Infoicon|goatm|big|link=Goat Milk}}\n |time = every 8 h\n}}\n'''Goats''' are [[farm]] [[animals]] that produce [[Goat Milk|goat milk]]. They are unlocked at [[experience]] level 32. They are the fifth and most expensive type of farm animal unlocked in the game.\n\nGender: Male\n\n{{Clr}}\n----\n==='''Appearance'''===\n<gallery>\nGoat.png|Goat\nGoat Full.png|Goat Full\nGoat Scared.png|Goat Scared\nGoat Fainting.png|Goat Fainting\nGoat Hungry.png|Goat Hungry\nFile:Goat Summer.png|Goat Summer\nFile:Goat Winter.png|Goat Winter\n</gallery>\n----\n==='''Alternate appearance'''===\n{{Main|Themes}}\nGoats wear themed clothes and accessories during summer, Halloween and winter.\n----\n==='''Buying'''===\n[[File:Goat Yard.png|150px|left|A goat yard]]\nGoats must be placed in [[Goat Yard|goat yards]] to be purchased. Yards cost 1,000 {{Infoicon|coin}} each. They are unlocked at levels 32, 37 and 50. Each yard can house four goats.\n\nAt level 32 goats cost 2,150 coins each; at level 37 5,400 coins; at level 50 8,650 coins.\n\nGoats and goat yards can be bought from the [[shop]].{{Infoicon|shop|bigger|link=Shop}}\n\n{{Clr}}\n----\n==='''Harvesting'''===\n[[File:Milk Bucket.png|150px|left|Milk bucket]]\nGoat milk can be collected from goats every 8 hours. Players can skip the wait by paying 10 [[diamond]]s per goat. Players must then give goats [[Goat Feed|goat feed]] to get another harvest.\n\nGoat feed is made of:\n{| border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"text-align: center; margin: .5em 0;\"\n|-\n|[[File:Corn.png|75px|Corn|link=Corn]]\n|[[File:Wheat.png|75px|Wheat|link=Wheat]]\n|[[File:Carrot.png|75px|Carrot|link=Carrot]]\n|-\n|'''x1'''\n|'''x1'''\n|'''x2'''\n|}\n----\n==='''Strategy tips'''===\n*It takes 40 minutes to make 3 units of [[Goat Feed|goat feed]]. You can easily collect all your milk and replenish your feed stock by the time the goats are ready to be milked again.\n* Goat milk can quite easily be found in the [[Daily Dirt]] but sells quickly. Selling it at maximum price is recommended.\n* Feeding farm animals and harvesting goat milk are common tasks in [[Derby|derbies]].\n----\n==='''Easter egg'''===\nTapping the goat yard or making a rock explode causes the goats to faint for a few seconds, then get back up and act normally. [[wikipedia:Fainting_goat|Fainting Goats]] (or \"Myotonic Goats\") exist in real life. This rare breed falls over with stiff legs for about 10 seconds when startled or excited.\n\n{{Clr}}\n----\n\n{{Navigation}}\n{{Languages\n|de = Ziege\n|es = Cabra\n|fr = Chèvre\n|it = Capra\n|no = Geit\n|sv = Get\n}}\n[[pt-br:Cabra]]\n\n[[Category:Farm Animals]]",
